WEBVTT

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.890
Ayumi-<i>san</i>?

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.380
If I'm wrong, you can hit me!

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.120
I'm coming inside!

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:27.570
This can't be real...

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.920
Tell me it's not real!

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.040
Ayumi-<i>san</i>!

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:41.100
Damn it!

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:16.490
"Episode 5: Spiral of Tragedy"

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.310
I need to do something.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.290
There has to be a way.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.020
Dad...

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:38.370
For the first time in my life,

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.220
I'm grateful to you.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.080
Okay, I'm passing out the questions.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:54.270
Good.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.150
Hey!

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:56.190
Boss!

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:56.980
Wait!

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:59.570
Weren't you really excited to take the test?

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:01.950
Hey, if you want to cut class,

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.990
you're not supposed to
just walk out in the middle of it!

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.450
There should be some way.

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:10.970
Some way to save her...

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:12.900
Some way...

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.090
Toyotomi-<i>kun</i>...

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:19.520
Chief... No, Ayumi.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:24.800
With my help, you can make
your little problem go away...

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:27.180
No! Don't!

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.390
This isn't right!

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:33.600
If you refuse me,
you'll be fired from Geotech.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.320
You won't be able to continue your research.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:41.810
And then you'll be out on the street, right?

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:45.990
What will happen to your son's future, then?

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:51.950
Kodai-<i>san</i>...

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.450
Ayumi-<i>san</i>!

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.220
Takuya-<i>kun</i>?

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:03.550
Toyotomi, you...

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:07.010
Sheesh. You need to show
some respect for her privacy.

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:09.100
Have some common decency--

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:11.390
Toyotomi-<i>kun</i>!

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:13.190
Takuya-<i>kun</i>, stop it!

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:16.270
Ayumi-<i>san</i>, you don't need to listen
to a word this asshole says.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.400
--What the hell is wrong with you?
--Come with me.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:23.280
Stop it, Takuya-<i>kun</i>.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:25.360
I'll take care of this.

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:27.950
You don't need to feel responsibility.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:29.490
Hey, wait!

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:32.160
You can't expect to get away with this!

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:35.670
Let me go!

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.490
How did this happen?

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:46.760
Don't come back.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:49.010
Never bother us again.

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:51.390
This is assault!

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:54.710
No, it's felony assault,
which is even worse!

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:58.060
I'll see you in jail for this!

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.200
Whatever.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.400
Just you wait!

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:05.240
In the end, the good guys always win!

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.500
Okay, that takes care of that.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.550
Ayumi-<i>san</i>.

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:31.310
Why...

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.140
Ayumi-<i>san</i>?

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:35.060
Why...

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:37.900
Why did this happen?

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:41.980
I'm changing this.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.490
This reality is bullshit.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:46.400
And I'm changing it!

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:54.680
--Okay, I'm passing out the questions.
--Okay!

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:55.830
Hey!

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:57.080
Boss!

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:57.920
Wait!

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.290
Weren't you really excited to take the test?

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:04.050
What's his problem?
He looked like death itself.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:05.630
Did he need to go to the bathroom?

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:08.470
It was probably number 
two from the look of it.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:15.680
Chief... No, Ayumi.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:19.980
With my help, you can make
your little problem go away...

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:23.690
Takuya-<i>kun</i>!

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:25.920
Sheesh. You need to show
some respect for her privacy.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.150
Let's go, Ayumi-<i>san</i>.

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:30.780
Wait, Takuya-<i>kun</i>.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:32.620
--That hurts... You're hurting me!

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:34.410
--Hey, we're in the middle
of an important discussion!

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:40.060
What were you going to talk about
with your pants down, porn director?

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.820
I-It's none of your business.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:54.060
Let me go, Takuya-<i>kun</i>!

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:55.560
Let me go!

00:06:57.890 --> 00:06:59.910
There's a reason...

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.190
There's a reason for this.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:04.950
Listen to me, Ayumi-<i>san</i>.

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:08.440
This was all a setup by Toyotomi.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:11.140
Those yakuza that attacked you.

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:13.570
The secret files that were stolen.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:15.140
It was all him!

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:17.870
Don't lie to me.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.350
It's not a lie!

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.900
Do you have proof? Do you?

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:25.580
Well...

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:29.740
Takuya-<i>kun</i>, you don't understand anything.

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:35.180
Toyotomi-<i>kun</i> is just trying to help us
out of the kindness of his heart.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:38.380
I believe in him.

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:41.730
You believe a guy who was about to rape you?

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:42.980
That's insane!

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:45.610
Ayumi-<i>san</i>, get a hold of yourself!

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:46.790
Why?

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:54.530
Why won't you understand?

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.010
Why...

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:04.850
Forget it.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.200
Ayumi

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:09.460
is just tired now...

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:21.230
Hey, are you okay?

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:23.140
The police! Call the police!

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:24.190
Hurry!

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:31.600
Ayumi-<i>san</i>...

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:36.290
I'm going to save you, 
no matter what it takes!

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:44.460
Okay, I'm passing out the questions.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:48.250
Boss?

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:50.130
What's wrong, Arima-<i>kun</i>?

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:53.210
Wait! Arima!

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:56.990
What's gotten into him?

00:08:57.340 --> 00:08:58.930
Did he need to go to the bathroom?

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:02.310
From the look of it, he already went...

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:06.850
Beating up Toyotomi didn't work.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.910
Taking Ayumi-<i>san</i> away didn't work.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:11.390
What's left?

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:21.240
Hey, if it isn't Arima-<i>kun</i>.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:23.230
Haven't seen you for a while.

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:26.460
Yuki, was that his name?

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.920
The little shrimp isn't with you today?

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:31.880
Sorry. I don't have time for this now.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:35.010
Come on, don't be so cold.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:42.600
--It's time for payback...
--...for what you did last time.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:46.060
You bastards... are in my way!

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:09.730
Ayumi-<i>san</i>?

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:29.940
One more time!

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:38.890
Ayumi-<i>san</i>!

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:47.680
Ayumi-<i>san</i>...

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:51.160
What can I do to save you?

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:55.560
What can I do?

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:01.330
The capabilities of the
Reflector Device are limited.

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:05.160
When the phenomenological density
of a certain world is extremely high,

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:08.080
if you approach its limit radius,

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:10.450
it becomes impossible to avoid.

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:15.250
This limit radius is referred to as
an "Event Schwarzschild Radius,"

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:20.010
"Fate"

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:18.440
and the unavoidable situation
is referred to as "fate."

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:22.990
Is this "fate"?

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.010
The hell it is.

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:30.390
I refuse to let fate

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:33.930
determine my life!

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:46.690
Oh, is that you, Takuya-<i>kun</i>?

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:48.840
I knew it!

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:53.250
What's wrong? You look so upset...

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:56.830
I've been waiting, Kaori-<i>san</i>.

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:58.090
"Be careful around Toyotomi."

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:00.600
A blue card...

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:15.320
It's a little too convenient that
you're offering me that blue card.

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:17.020
It's simple.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:20.090
I just tried to think what somebody who was

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:23.210
sniffing around Geotech would want most.

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:25.220
That business card I gave you...

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:28.990
You want to know what
Toyotomi's been up to.

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:30.760
You're pretty quick on the uptake, too.

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:32.660
Sure.

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:35.990
I'll tell you in exchange for the blue card.

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:39.040
Just give me a second.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:42.360
I know it's somewhere around here.

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:43.560
Here.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.150
Th-This is...

00:13:51.610 --> 00:13:54.270
Well? Think it'll help?

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:56.370
Yeah. Thanks.

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:59.560
I like that face much better.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.230
You look just like your father.

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:04.030
You know just what to say
to make somebody feel good.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:07.020
You look even more like him when you're mad.

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:09.810
Bye.

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:12.970
Oh, Kaori-<i>san</i>.

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:14.700
What?

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:17.820
You want to have some fun with me?

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:20.040
No!

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:20.790
Oh?

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:23.800
You're awfully calm, considering
a babe like me is offering herself to you.

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:25.380
A babe?

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:28.590
Where are you, babe? Come on out!

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.470
So that's how it's gonna be, huh?

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:39.650
I always wanted to take a boy's virginity.

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:42.610
Sorry. I'm not a virgin.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:44.270
Oh, you're not?

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:45.780
Too bad.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:48.950
Oh, right.

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:52.030
What's in the place protected 
by the blue card?

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:55.750
I'll tell you later, so you'll have
something to look forward to.

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:19.980
Okay, I'm passing out the questions.

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:20.910
Okay!

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:23.560
Boss!

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:24.480
Wait!

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:27.030
Weren't you really excited to take the test?

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:30.200
Sensei?

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:31.530
Leave him be.

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:34.030
Okay, let's get started!

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:38.830
Come on, Ayumi!

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:39.700
No!

00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:46.210
Sheesh. You need to show
some respect for her privacy.

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:49.840
Have some common decency, why don't you?

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:53.590
Ayumi-<i>san</i>, there's no need
to listen to a thing he says.

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:58.370
That whole thing where the yakuza
attacked you was a setup, by him!

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:02.310
I don't know anything about any yakuza.

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:05.770
Takuya, you can't go around
telling lies about people.

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:07.500
Got any proof?

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:11.080
I sure do. Right here.

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:15.660
This is impossible.

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:17.330
How...

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:19.460
Where did you get this?

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:23.240
Toyotomi-<i>kun</i>, what are these pictures?

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:25.290
What's going on?

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:28.220
Give it up, Toyotomi.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:30.630
You're not talking your way out of this.

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:39.500
What are you laughing about?

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:45.850
I gave a used-up old widow like her
a shot at a young, handsome man like me.

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:47.940
She should be thanking me!

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:49.480
You bastard--

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:50.320
Bye!

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:51.610
Shit!

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:52.610
I'm not letting you get away!

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:54.190
Stop right there!

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:02.610
Wait!

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.330
Give it up already!

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:07.920
I told you, I'm not 
interested in that old hag!

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:11.920
I'll see you in jail for this!

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:13.010
No way!

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:15.300
In the end, the good guys always win!

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:20.420
Hi there!

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:22.540
Kaori-<i>san</i>?

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:25.350
I just grabbed a pot to hit him with.

00:17:25.350 --> 00:17:26.520
Will it be okay?

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:28.230
Be okay...

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:30.520
Are you talking about
the pot itself? Or Toyotomi?

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:32.570
The pot. Of course.

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:34.030
Of course.

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:38.280
He pissed me off,
so I always wanted to do this.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:39.830
What a great stress buster!

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:40.660
You know?

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:43.440
I see.

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:49.630
Given what's going on with Ayumi-<i>san</i>,
I can't recommend going to the police.

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:51.090
Why?

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:57.010
The media's about to report that
she sold secret data to a rival company.

00:17:57.290 --> 00:17:59.970
But that's just a fake rumor.

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:03.820
Gossip and mean rumors
make perfect bait for viewers.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:06.770
But does that mean we let him go?

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:10.950
Of course, this loser needs dealt with.

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:14.280
Can you let me take care of this?

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:18.240
Fine.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:20.970
Get back to your mom.

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:23.440
That's right. Ayumi-<i>san</i>...

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.580
Okay, take care of it!

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:26.700
Sure thing.

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:29.170
I'm back!

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:31.360
Ayumi-<i>san</i>!

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:42.850
No way...

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:49.840
Kodai-<i>san</i>.

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:51.550
I'm sorry.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:55.420
Ayumi just...

00:18:56.510 --> 00:18:57.550
can't go on...

00:18:59.180 --> 00:18:59.910
Ayumi-<i>san</i>!

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:02.650
Takuya-<i>kun</i>...

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:05.370
Don't be stupid.

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:07.160
Come on! Give me the razor!

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:14.730
Stay back.

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:18.090
Ayumi

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:21.930
doesn't need to live anymore...

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:24.180
Who decided that?

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:27.950
I just decided it now.

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:32.670
Kodai-<i>san</i>...

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:36.860
Ayumi is coming to be with you.

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:39.610
Stop it!

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:41.860
Get off me!

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:42.570
Be careful with that thing!

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.950
No! Let me go!

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:48.540
Do you really think I'm going to do that?

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:50.960
Do what your mother tells you to!

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:52.880
Hell no!

00:19:58.340 --> 00:19:59.330
Ayumi-<i>san</i>...

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:02.470
Think about what you're doing a little more.

00:20:04.090 --> 00:20:06.430
What do you know?

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:07.140
You're just a kid!

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:14.280
You hit me...

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:17.070
You hit Ayumi!

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:21.280
It's the best way to make
a child stop throwing a tantrum.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:25.030
What do you know about Ayumi?

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:26.830
I know your underwear measurements.

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:29.840
Dummy! Dummy! Dummy!

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:34.770
Ayumi hurts so much...
She's so lonely she could die!

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:36.710
I know!

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:38.090
You don't!

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:44.690
Maybe I don't, but...

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:47.550
Why don't you get madder?

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:56.740
Don't be stupid, Ayumi.
You know better than this.

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:01.650
Well? That sounded a little like him, right?

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:09.990
Why... Why aren't you anything alike
even though you're father and son?

00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:11.620
It didn't sound like him, huh?

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:13.520
I was pretty sure it did.

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.390
Well? Fell better?

00:21:19.710 --> 00:21:21.730
Yes. I'm sorry.

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:25.940
I'll prove your innocence.

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:31.280
And then you can go back to your research.

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:35.730
Takuya-<i>kun</i>, how much do you
know about what's going on?

00:21:38.520 --> 00:21:43.520
Even if I end up going to
another time or another world...

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:46.310
I'll save you as many times as I have to.

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:51.890
So believe in me.

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:54.630
And never do this again.

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:56.880
Can you promise me that?

00:21:59.390 --> 00:22:00.000
Yeah.

00:22:01.300 --> 00:22:02.500
I promise.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:41.570
"Episode 6: Beyond a Pale Light"

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:39.180
Episode 6: "Beyond a Pale Light."
